# Per-app site file for the shared edge Caddy. edge.sh substitutes the two
# placeholders and installs the result as /root/caddy/sites/<slug>.caddy, which
# the top-level Caddyfile imports.
#
# Both blue/green colors are listed; exactly one runs at a time (story 7.2). A
# dial to the stopped color's name fails instantly, fail_duration marks it down,
# and lb_try_* retries the live one — so requests are held through the swap
# window instead of dropped.
#
# The upstream names are the app's per-color aliases on the shared `edge`
# network (compose.yaml). They carry the app slug because every app on this
# droplet shares that network: a bare `app_blue` would be ambiguous, and Caddy
# would round-robin traffic into the wrong tenant.
__DOMAIN__ {
	reverse_proxy __SLUG__-blue:4000 __SLUG__-green:4000 {
		lb_try_duration 30s
		lb_try_interval 250ms
		fail_duration 10s
	}
}
